    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d836">

                <pb facs="0904" n="784" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg784"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.48 Earthquake of 1931/17: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hanna</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-04-01T11:00:00-05:00">April 1, 1931—11
                    a.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>27. The American Red Cross requests you to express its deepest sympathy to
                    President Moncada.</p>
                <p>With reference to Beaulac’s comment<anchor n="6" xml:id="d836-f1"/> regarding
                    insufficiency of the $10,000 already advanced by the Red Cross you are informed
                    that Mr. Swift will make recommendations with respect to further requirements.
                    In utilizing this sum draw separate drafts and render separate account.</p>
                <p>The Department extends its deepest sympathy to the members of the Legation.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Carr</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d836-f1" n="6" xml:id="d836-f1-content">
                <p>See telegram received April 1, 1:40 a.m., from the Chargé in Nicaragua; <ref
                        target="#pg783">p. 783</ref>.</p>
            </note>
